sparsity, Grouped-Subspace Latent Attention, and running intelligence on local NPU silicon."}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-12","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 lg:gap-12 items-start","children":[["$","aside",null,{"className":"lg:col-span-3 lg:sticky lg:top-24 space-y-8 font-mono text-xs border-b lg:border-b-0 lg:border-r border-ink-dark/10 dark:border-paper-100/10 pb-8 lg:pb-0 pr-0 lg:pr-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-[10px] text-accent font-bold uppercase tracking-widest","children":"CHAPTER OUTLINE"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-2 text-ink-dark/80 dark:text-paper-200/80 text-[11px]","children":[["$","li","the-monolith-trap",{"className":"hover:text-accent transition-colors","children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#the-monolith-trap","className":"block leading-snug","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-mono mr-1.5","children":["0",1,"."]}],"I. The Monolith Trap"]}]}],["$","li","grouped-subspace-latent-attention",{"className":"hover:text-accent transition-colors","children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#grouped-subspace-latent-attention","className":"block leading-snug","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-mono mr-1.5","children":["0",2,"."]}],"II. Grouped-Subspace Latent Attention"]}]}],["$","li","local-npu-or-bust",{"className":"hover:text-accent transition-colors","children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#local-npu-or-bust","className":"block leading-snug","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-mono mr-1.5","children":["0",3,"."]}],"III. Local NPU or Bust"]}]}],["$","li","the-virtue-of-constraints",{"className":"hover:text-accent transition-colors","children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#the-virtue-of-constraints","className":"block leading-snug","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-mono mr-1.5","children":["0",4,"."]}],"IV. The Virtue of Constraints"]}]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-2 pt-4 border-t border-ink-dark/10 dark:border-paper-100/10 text-[10px] text-ink-muted","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":["AUTHOR: ","Matthew Chen"," (","陳軍宇",")"]}],["$","div",null,{"children":["LOCATION: ","Jiuru / Tamsui, Taiwan"]}],["$","div",null,{"children":["MOOD: ",["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-bold uppercase","children":"Defiant"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"pt-2","children":["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/Ch3nOff","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","className":"underline hover:text-accent","children":"GitHub @Ch3nOff"}]}]]}]]}],["$","main",null,{"className":"lg:col-span-6 space-y-12","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"drop-cap font-sans text-lg sm:text-xl text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-100 leading-relaxed font-light","children":"There is an unspoken sickness in contemporary machine learning: the belief that intelligence is purely a function of linear parameter scaling. If your model fails at multi-step deductive routing, the industry answer is almost comical — throw another thirty billion parameters into the feed-forward layers, rent eight more racks in Ohio, and bill the venture fund. I reject this premise entirely."}],[["$","section","0",{"id":"the-monolith-trap","className":"space-y-6 pt-4 scroll-mt-28","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-50 tracking-tight border-b border-ink-dark/15 dark:border-paper-100/15 pb-2","children":"I. The Monolith Trap"}],"$undefined",[["$","p","0",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"When you train a monolithic dense transformer, every single token pays the exact same thermodynamic tax. Whether the model is predicting the next letter in an arithmetic proof or outputting a generic punctuation mark, all layers activate simultaneously. This is not how biological synapses operate, nor is it how economical computing survives."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"In my experiments with small language models (SLMs) in the 250M to 750M range, I noticed something remarkable: when you constrain capacity, the network is forced to learn structural representations rather than surface-level token memorization. It stops being a search engine in disguise and starts acting like an algorithmic engine."}]],["$","figure",null,{"className":"my-8 py-6 border-y-2 border-accent/40 px-4 sm:px-6 bg-accent/5 dark:bg-accent/10","children":["$","blockquote",null,{"className":"font-serif italic text-xl sm:text-2xl text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-50 leading-snug","children":["“","Constraints are not limitations; they are the only reason elegance exists in engineering.","”"]}]}],"$undefined","$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"lg:hidden p-3 bg-accent/5 border-l-2 border-accent font-hand text-accent text-sm","children":["Note: ","Why carry an encyclopedia in your pocket when you only need a chisel and a straightedge?"]}]]}],["$","section","1",{"id":"grouped-subspace-latent-attention","className":"space-y-6 pt-4 scroll-mt-28","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-50 tracking-tight border-b border-ink-dark/15 dark:border-paper-100/15 pb-2","children":"II. Grouped-Subspace Latent Attention"}],"$undefined",[["$","p","0",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"The primary bottleneck on consumer chips isn't FLOPs — it is the memory bus. During autoregressive decoding, loading the KV-cache across memory channels throttles the processing units. Standard Multi-Head Attention is recklessly wasteful here."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"By decomposing the attention projections into grouped subspaces with low-rank factorization, we can compress the active memory footprint down to a fraction of standard MHA. The query vectors only look into specific latent subspaces conditioned on the routing token."}]],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"my-6 p-4 border border-ink-dark/20 dark:border-paper-100/20 bg-paper-100/60 dark:bg-paper-900/60 font-mono text-[10px] sm:text-xs overflow-x-auto text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-100","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"text-[9px] text-accent uppercase tracking-widest pb-2 mb-2 border-b border-ink-dark/10","children":"Subspace Routing Schematic"}],["$","pre",null,{"className":"leading-tight","children":"[Token In] ──► [Sparse Subspace Projector]\n                     │\n         ┌───────────┼───────────┐\n         ▼           ▼           ▼\n     Subspace 0  Subspace 1  Subspace N\n         │           │           │\n         └───────────┼───────────┘\n                     ▼\n        [Orthogonal Recomposition] ──► [Next Layer]"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"my-6 border border-ink-dark/20 dark:border-paper-100/20 bg-ink-pure text-paper-100 p-4 font-mono text-xs overflow-x-auto","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex justify-between items-center text-[9px] text-paper-200/60 pb-2 mb-2 border-b border-paper-100/10 uppercase tracking-widest","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":["LANGUAGE: ","python"]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"CH3NOFF KERNEL"}]]}],["$","pre",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"class SubspaceLatentRouter(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, d_model=512, n_subspaces=8, rank=32):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.n_subspaces = n_subspaces\n        self.down_proj = nn.Linear(d_model, n_subspaces * rank, bias=False)\n        self.up_proj = nn.Linear(rank, d_model, bias=False)\n        self.gate = nn.Parameter(torch.randn(n_subspaces))\n\n    def forward(self, x):\n        # Route dynamically without dense activation penalties\n        b, s, d = x.shape\n        subspaces = self.down_proj(x).view(b, s, self.n_subspaces, -1)\n        weights = F.softmax(self.gate, dim=-1)\n        routed = torch.einsum('bsnr,n->bsr', subspaces, weights)\n        return self.up_proj(routed)"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"text-[9px] text-paper-200/50 pt-2 mt-2 border-t border-paper-100/10 italic","children":["// ","Minimal prototype of grouped latent routing tested in PyTorch"]}]]}],"$undefined"]}],["$","section","2",{"id":"local-npu-or-bust","className":"space-y-6 pt-4 scroll-mt-28","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-50 tracking-tight border-b border-ink-dark/15 dark:border-paper-100/15 pb-2","children":"III. Local NPU or Bust"}],"$undefined",[["$","p","0",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"I want my AI agents to live on my desk, not in a server room in North Virginia. When an agent runs locally — wired to a local serial port, monitoring system logs, listening to an audio buffer — the latency drops from 450 milliseconds down to 14 milliseconds."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"At 14ms, interaction ceases to be an RPC request and becomes a continuous biological feedback loop. You feel the machine reacting before your fingertips have fully lifted from the mechanical switches."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"lg:hidden p-3 bg-accent/5 border-l-2 border-accent font-hand text-accent text-sm","children":["Note: ","When latency hits under 20ms, software begins to feel like a musical instrument."]}]]}],["$","section","3",{"id":"the-virtue-of-constraints","className":"space-y-6 pt-4 scroll-mt-28","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-50 tracking-tight border-b border-ink-dark/15 dark:border-paper-100/15 pb-2","children":"IV. The Virtue of Constraints"}],"$undefined",[["$","p","0",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"We have traded intellectual discipline for brute force compute. Building Small Language Models forces you to inspect every layer, question every tensor allocation, and optimize every activation function."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"font-sans text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-dark/90 dark:text-paper-100/90 leading-relaxed font-normal","children":"This isn't about nostalgia for slow hardware. It's about self-reliance. An intelligence that fits on a USB drive and runs on battery power is sovereign; an intelligence tethered to a subscription token is just an API lease."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]],["$","footer",null,{"className":"pt-12 border-t border-ink-dark/20 dark:border-paper-100/20 space-y-4 font-mono text-xs","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"text-[10px] text-accent uppercase tracking-widest font-bold","children":"[FOOTNOTES & FORMAL CITATIONS]"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"space-y-2 list-decimal list-inside text-ink-muted text-[11px]","children":[["$","li","1",{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":["$","span",null,{"className":"text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-100 font-sans","children":"Monolithic models waste upwards of 82% of activations on inert semantic tokens during simple inductive reasoning tasks."}]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":["$","span",null,{"className":"text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-100 font-sans","children":"Grouped-Subspace Latent Attention projects the key-value cache into orthogonal low-rank sub-manifolds, reducing memory bandwidth by 3.8x."}]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":["$","span",null,{"className":"text-ink-dark dark:text-paper-100 font-sans","children":"Testing conducted on Intel Core Ultra & RTX 40/50 series laptop silicon utilizing custom Triton and PyTorch NPU kernels."}]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","aside",null,{"className":"hidden lg:block lg:col-span-3 space-y-8 font-mono text-xs border-l border-ink-dark/10 dark:border-paper-100/10 pl-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-[10px] text-accent font-bold uppercase tracking-widest block","children":"MARGINALIA & NOTES"}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"p-3 bg-paper-100/50 dark:bg-paper-900/50 border border-ink-dark/10 dark:border-paper-100/10 space-y-1 relative","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-[8px] text-accent uppercase tracking-widest block","children":["ANNOTATION § 0",1]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"margin-hand text-base text-accent","children":["“","Why carry an encyclopedia in your pocket when you only need a chisel and a straightedge?","”"]}]]}],null,["$","div","2",{"className":"p-3 bg-paper-100/50 dark:bg-paper-900/50 border border-ink-dark/10 dark:border-paper-100/10 space-y-1 relative","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-[8px] text-accent uppercase tracking-widest block","children":["ANNOTATION § 0",3]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"margin-hand text-base text-accent","children":["“","When latency hits under 20ms, software begins to feel like a musical instrument.","”"]}]]}],null],["$","div",null,{"className":"p-4 border border-ink-dark/15 dark:border-paper-100/15 bg-paper-100/30 text-[10px] space-y-2","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"text-accent uppercase font-bold tracking-widest","children":"PERSONAL DISCIPLINE"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-sans text-ink-dark/80 dark:text-paper-200/80 leading-normal","children":"All code samples and algorithmic theorems are tested on real silicon before archiving."}]]}]]}]]}]}]]}],null],null],null]},[null,["$","$L4",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","article","children","$5","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorSty